      "finding": "Rejects variable-focus two-objective arrangement as inconvenient; modifies prior double-branch caliper with curved short arms to clear the disk. Long arms eight or ten times short; tips close together, focal-plane alignment and screw clamp described. Prior Tables p71 cited without edition identification. No physical instrument examined."
    },
    {
      "locator": "pp62-63/canvases174-175",
      "finding": "Describes target calibration: three/four parallel black marks with two-inch center spacing, target at measured200/300toises, orientation controls and measured long-arm opening. Right-triangle tangent calculation described; no executed trial data or uncertainties supplied. Historical units retained without assumed conversion."
    },
    {
      "locator": "pp64-66/canvases176-178",
      "finding": "Equilateral triangle card divided into24parts for half-digits; source explicitly says figure shows only12 to avoid clutter. Parallel cross-line scales measured disk diameter, enabling relative eclipse phases without angular-diameter tables. Remaining luminous width must be complemented to12digits. Separate24arcminute calibration and estimated twelfths give5arcsecond reading subdivisions, not measured accuracy."
    },
    {
      "locator": "p67/canvas179",
      "finding": "Reports visibility difficulty against dark sky, proposes white silk in front of objective to resemble light cloud, and claims experience. Historical practice only, not a modern observing recommendation or calibrated demonstration. Construction article ends; de la Faye water-raising article starts on same page."
    },
